  "prompt": "Find the common rule that maps an input grid to an output grid, given the examples below. Generate a python script that takes a grid as input and transforms it according to the this rule. Anticipate that this program will be applied to several grids, not only the shown test grid.\n\nYour script must define exactly one callable entrypoint:\ndef solve(grid):\nwhere `grid` is passed as a list of lists of integers (list[list[int]]) and the function returns the transformed grid in the same format.\n\nExample 1:\n\nInput:\n1 1 1\n2 2 2\n1 1 1\nOutput:\n1\n2\n1\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput:\n3 4 6\n3 4 6\n3 4 6\nOutput:\n3 4 6\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput:\n2 3 3 8 1\n2 3 3 8 1\n2 3 3 8 1\nOutput:\n2 3 8 1\n\nExample 4:\n\nInput:\n2 2\n6 6\n8 8\n8 8\nOutput:\n2\n6\n8\n\nExample 5:\n\nInput:\n4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4\n2 2 2 2\n2 2 2 2\n8 8 8 8\n3 3 3 3\nOutput:\n4\n2\n8\n3\n\nBelow is a test input grid.\n\nInput:\n1 1 2 3 3 3 8 8 4\n1 1 2 3 3 3 8 8 4\n1 1 2 3 3 3 8 8 4\n1 1 2 3 3 3 8 8 4\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    if rows == 0:\n        return []\n    \n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Check if all rows are identical\n    first_row = grid[0]\n    all_rows_same = True\n    for r in range(1, rows):\n        if grid[r] != first_row:\n            all_rows_same = False\n            break\n    \n    if all_rows_same:\n        # Compress horizontally: remove consecutive duplicates\n        result = []\n        for val in first_row:\n            if not result or result[-1] != val:\n                result.append(val)\n        return [result]\n    \n    # Check if all columns are identical\n    first_col = [grid[r][0] for r in range(rows)]\n    all_cols_same = True\n    for c in range(1, cols):\n        current_col = [grid[r][c] for r in range(rows)]\n        if current_col != first_col:\n            all_cols_same = False\n            break\n    \n    if all_cols_same:\n        # Compress vertically: remove consecutive duplicates\n        result = []\n        for val in first_col:\n            if not result or result[-1] != val:\n                result.append(val)\n        # Return as column vector\n        return [[val] for val in result]\n    \n    return grid\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    if rows == 0:\n        return []\n    \n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Check if all rows are identical\n    first_row = grid[0]\n    all_rows_same = True\n    for r in range(1, rows):\n        if grid[r] != first_row:\n            all_rows_same = False\n            break\n    \n    if all_rows_same:\n        # Compress horizontally: remove consecutive duplicates\n        result = []\n        for val in first_row:\n            if not result or result[-1] != val:\n                result.append(val)\n        return [result]\n    \n    # Check if all columns are identical\n    first_col = [grid[r][0] for r in range(rows)]\n    all_cols_same = True\n    for c in range(1, cols):\n        current_col = [grid[r][c] for r in range(rows)]\n        if current_col != first_col:\n            all_cols_same = False\n            break\n    \n    if all_cols_same:\n        # Compress vertically: remove consecutive duplicates\n        result = []\n        for val in first_col:\n            if not result or result[-1] != val:\n                result.append(val)\n        # Return as column vector\n        return [[val] for val in result]\n    \n    return grid",
